<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Emre Taşar, a software engineer focused on C++, Qt, and dependable systems.">
  <article class="max-w-2xl prose-content">
    <p class="font-mono text-sm text-stone-500 dark:text-zinc-400">About</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-950 dark:text-zinc-50">I enjoy learning new things, writing code and having an impact in the fields I have been working.</h1>
    <p>I’m a software engineer with professional experience in modern C++ and Qt application development for defense and autonomous systems. My work spans embedded communication interfaces, desktop applications, and UAV ground control systems.</p>
    <p>I care about software that is reliable in practice: clear interfaces, maintainable code, careful integration, and development processes that make quality repeatable. I’m also growing my backend engineering skills and exploring how sound system design translates across platforms.</p>
    <h2>What I work with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Modern C++ (C++14/17/20)</li>
      <li>Object-Oriented Programming</li>
      <li>Design Patterns</li>
      <li>Qt/QML desktop applications and Linux-based ground control systems</li>
      <li>TCP/IP, UDP, MIL-STD-1553, and MAVLink communication protocols</li>
      <li>GitLab CI/CD, CppCheck, and SonarQube quality workflows</li>
      <li>Backend technologies including Django, Flask, FastAPI, Node.js</li>
      <li>Relational and NoSQL Databases</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>I develop and customize Linux-based ground control software at my previous job, working with QGroundControl, PX4, MAVLink, and software-in-the-loop simulation. Before that, I developed C++ communication interfaces between embedded systems and contributed to CI/CD and static-analysis practices.</p>
    <p>I hold a BSc in Computer Engineering from Istanbul Technical University. Earlier research and internship work also introduced me to computer vision and image processing.</p>
  </article>
